    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a2">

                <pb facs="0133" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg43"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    809.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fellner to Mr.
                            Jay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial and Royal Ministry of Commerce,<lb/>Universal Exposition
                                Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-08-31"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August</hi> 31, 1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The ministry of commerce has the honor to transmit to the honorable legation two
                    official notes, intended for the commission of the United States of America for
                    the Vienna Universal Exposition, 1873, relative to the presentation of the
                    prizes awarded at the Universal Exposition, 1873, in Vienna to exhibitors, and
                    to respectfully request that these notes, together with the accompanying
                    diplomas and-medals, may be sent by the earliest occasion that may offer to the
                    commission of the United States of America, for which courtesy the legation is
                    solicited to accept the thanks of the ministry of commerce.</p>
                <p>For the imperial and royal ministry of commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed>FELLNER.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To the honorable <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation at
                            Vienna.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
